# Load the SKY130 technology into Magic.
#
# Magic reads .magicrc from the directory you start it in. Without this file
# Magic comes up with its own toy technology, every SKY130 layer is missing,
# and the error you get ("Failed to load technology") does not say why.
#
# The workbench image also ships a ~/.magicrc that loads the same PDK file. If
# it already did so, loading it a second time collides on the GUI-only line
# `rename closewrapper closewrapperonly` inside sky130A.tcl, and Magic prints
#     Error parsing ".magicrc": can't rename to "closewrapperonly": command already exists
#     Bad local startup file ".magicrc", continuing without.
# in the first two lines of your console - which looks exactly like the broken
# toolchain this course teaches you to recognise, on a toolchain that is fine.
# So only load it if nothing has loaded it yet.
if {[tech name] eq "sky130A"} {
    # Already loaded by ~/.magicrc. Nothing to do.
} elseif {[info exists env(PDK_ROOT)]} {
    source $env(PDK_ROOT)/sky130A/libs.tech/magic/sky130A.magicrc
} else {
    puts stderr "PDK_ROOT is not set. Try:  export PDK_ROOT=/foss/pdks"
}
